This repository builds and redistributes upstream toolchain components.
The build layer (Dockerfile, build-sysroot.sh, export-sysroot.sh, the
emcc/em++/emrun wrappers produced by the export, and toolchain/*.cmake)
is MIT-licensed. See LICENSE.

Upstream components are pinned in upstream-commits.txt:

  clang-p2996   Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
                https://github.com/bloomberg/clang-p2996
                commit f72d85e5a0fd9c960b07b6f1c8875110701cb627
  emscripten    MIT License and the University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source License
                https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten
                tag 4.0.21
  binaryen      Apache License 2.0
                https://github.com/WebAssembly/binaryen
                commit ecf25d6e6d20d2018c4897dcf95babdb16e7d311
                (wasm-opt reports this as version_125-5-gecf25d6e6)
  Node.js       MIT License
  Debian 12     various free-software licenses; see Debian's copyright files

Our patch is not a fork of those trees. The Dockerfile checks out the pins,
builds them, then replaces emscripten's libcxx with clang-p2996's libcxx so
that `^^` reflection can compile to WebAssembly. Emscripten's wasm-specific
libcxx files are copied back on top of that replacement: __config_site,
__config_site.in, __assertion_handler, new.cpp, and overridable_function.h.
Those steps are the libcxx replacement block in the Dockerfile.
